# port-patches.sh: glm/series @ 14e8577b6303 over glm/zig-engine-base @ 0db3e2f6652b (commits d9d631748d76..2a16b14a4903); regenerate with scripts/port-patches.sh, do not edit
server + core: a long prompt's preparation no longer runs rank 0 out of memory (port of DeepSeek 0023, GLM's three renders)

The template's render and the tokenizer's encode and decode built their
scratch arenas on the caller's allocator, the server's request arena, so
nothing they freed went back until the request ended. With the prompt cache
on, a GLM request is rendered and tokenized three times (the prompt, its
history and the rewind probe): on a long agent conversation with the GLM
template the request's arena grew by ~1,200-1,900 bytes a text byte (4.9 GB
for 3.9 MiB of text), and a few long resumes at once could take a GB10's
MemAvailable to zero on rank 0.

- core: render's, encode's and decode's scratch come from the page
  allocator; only the text and the ids come from the caller's.
  Pre-tokenization walks depth first (the same ids).
- server/prepare_gate.zig: each prepare reserves 48 bytes a text byte; while
  others are in flight a prepare waits if MemAvailable less their
  reservations would fall under the floor. One with none in flight always
  goes; a waiting one whose client leaves is cancelled; without
  /proc/meminfo it lets everything through.
- GLM's kept reasoning (TF_GLM_KEEP_REASONING) is signed in one pass instead
  of once a step inside every render (quadratic: ~655 bytes a text byte at
  380 KiB), and chat.prepare restores it once, before the gate, so the gate
  counts it.
- A kept-alive connection's arena keeps at most 1 MiB and is reset once a
  request is answered.

Switch: TENSORFOLD_PREPARE_FLOOR_GIB (rank 0; GiB, default 3; 0 turns the gate
off). The reservation is a host measurement on the shipped GLM template with a
GLM-like byte-level BPE (30-46 bytes a text byte; 673.6 before the one-pass
signer); replies unchanged (test-golden 309/319 equal to the frozen Python
answers, 0 unexpected).

Measured on the pair: part of round 1's and round 2's images (g1, g2), every
feature off: exact 39/39 identical to the base engine, a 99,899-token prompt
included. Rank 0's RSS against the reservation is not measured on the pair
yet.

DeepSeek's fix (MiaAI-Lab/DeepSeek-v4.1-Flash-1017-2x-DGX-Sparks#40, there 24
bytes a text byte for two renders) adapted to GLM. A base-engine fix, also
offered alone (glm/pr-prepare-memory, the same bytes): whichever lands first,
the other copy is an exact duplicate.

Credits: Robert Wojciechowski (GitHub @wojo, X @rwojo).
Apply from the checkout root with: git apply 0015-zig-server-prepare-memory.patch

